  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1248 AM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nAn upper trough will deepen across the Great Lakes Region into \nthe Mid Atlantic Wednesday through Friday. Meanwhile, upper \nridging will build from the Central and Southern Rockies into \nthe High Plains. This will bring an amplified northwest flow the\nthe Central Plains. Highs will range from 53 to 63 Wednesday, \nwhich is still about 7 to 10 degrees above normal. Gusty \nnorthwest winds on Wednesday 15 to 30 mph, with some gusts to 35\nmph possible. Cooler air will be drawn in Thursday into Friday,\nespecially across the east. Winds will be lighter and highs \ncontrasting from the low 40s far northeast to upper 50s to near \n60 far western areas Thursday, then slightly warmer Friday with \na return of southerly winds. Upper ridging will return Saturday \ninto Sunday with highs returning to the low to mid 60s most \nlocations by Sunday. Lows will be coldest Wednesday night in the\nlow 30s and Thursday night in the upper 20s. Dry conditions \nwill persist Wednesday through Sunday.",
